{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfswqpxyEC9E5jMtJJabL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four rows are **MEANING**, and I would bless all four, so I re-attested them myself because the LLR/TC rung is released. Both commits went through the pre-commit checks with no failures.\n\n**Verdict** (`0dc57863`, trailer `WI: WI-854`, file `docs/reviews/wi-854/001-ADJUDICATE-8d43a5c.md`, `VERDICT: MEANING rows=4`):\n- **LLR-167 Detail:** adds the single question home (`prompts/spine-questions.md`). It is read at render time and picks question sections by tier. If the home is missing or can't serve the rows' tiers, the brief is refused and there is no fallback. A brief built to the old text, with questions written into the template or a fallback, would fail this.\n- **TC-161 Method:** adds tests for that home: tier selection, a combined brief carrying its rows' questions, a changed home changing the brief, the refusal cases, and no second copy of the questions anywhere.\n- **LLR-270 Detail:** an edit to the question home now drains a kept-warm adjudicator session, whenever a retained amendment, first-approval or combined brief uses it. Under the old text that session would have kept being resumed.\n- **TC-322 Method:** adds the check that the home is counted among the inputs that drain such a session.\n\n**Why I would bless them:** the new text follows from its parents, SR-146 (shipped, reviewable prompts) and SR-227 (drain when what the session judges under changes). Each row keeps to its own decision, and every new clause has a test. I ran the named tests: 19 passed in 10.92 s.\n\n**Re-attestation** (`43eeceef`, act 91): `intake.py snapshot --reattests LLR-167,TC-161,LLR-270,TC-322` copied the new text into `docs/archive/last_approved`. Nothing refused, and I edited no registry cells.\n\n**One separate gap, which needs a follow-up WI you would file:** the question home is shipped instruction text that goes into launched briefs, but the prompt catalogue (`prompts/CATALOG.md`, built from `KIT_PROMPTS`) doesn't list it. So editing the home changes no catalogued digest, and the catalogue's `--check` stays green. Each session's recorded prompt digest still changes, so SR-146's audit trail holds and SR-146's text needs no change. The fix is either:\n- list the home in the catalogue by digest, or\n- state in the catalogue's contract (IF-098) that composed fragments are left out, as IF-100 already does for the dual-plan hats.\n\nI didn't draft this as a `## Dispositions` block, because intake only reads those from adjudication-kind specs and WI-854's spec isn't one, so the block would never be minted. The finding is written up in the verdict file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":373,"cache_read_input_tokens":89002,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":373},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a511e73-e906-4589-9f31-ae73f8534ed7","uuid":"22ebff2b-419b-4ff8-bb7a-31afee899f06","timestamp":"2026-10-10T04:44:28.780Z","request_id":"req_011Cfswqpiq4WaDZ5WKmkQHy"}
